== contention-robust sample budgeting ==
a fast routine reaches the 64-sample cap: true
a stall burst cannot spend the budget before the 16-sample floor: true
a mostly stalled sample window reports contention: true
a window's reading is its minimum, not its sum or its mean: true
a refused positive timing cannot enter ranking or calibration: true
a contended calibration still gets the depth its estimate is owed: true
an unresolved zero clock window is refused by ranking without being called contention: true
queued contention is detected on raw batch wall before per-launch division: true
a consistently slow routine is not mistaken for host contention: true
the top-up budget accumulates per-sample time: true
a complete measurement set with a winner is cacheable: true
a contention-refused window prevents caching an incomplete winner: true
a search with no measured winner remains uncacheable: true
== queued batch depth ==
CUDA and HIP use the raised queue-depth cap: true
cc and Metal retain the historical queue-depth cap: true
every calibration estimate gets the depth the policy owes it: true
every degenerate calibration estimate is refused by ranking but still batched: true
no calibration estimate ever yields a depth below 1: true
no calibration estimate ever yields a depth above the cap: true
depth refinement removes fixed synchronization cost from launch scaling: true
over-target calibration requires a depth-separated marginal confirmation: true

== a depth-1 settle reuses its calibration ==
a window resumed after any prefix is the uninterrupted window: true

== a fitted single crossing keeps supported queued work ==
a supported batched slope keeps depth 2 despite a fitted single above the target: true
the boundary reading is the queued batch's per-launch cost, with no reused singles: true
the retained boundary depth is supported by two distinct batched probes: true
a fixed-dominated fit retains its refusal without the boundary floor: true
over-target or unresolved batched work remains unbatched and unranked: true
a comparison of supported boundary candidates can cache: true
one genuinely refused candidate still vetoes the whole comparison's cache: true
a fixed-dominated refusal still vetoes the comparison's cache: true
a slow candidate settles at depth 1 under either calibration: true
a depth-1 settle times no fresh window: its window is the calibration's singles: true
a reused window's reading is the per-launch time: true
the instrument counts a fresh window where one is timed: isolated dispatches its 16: true
at depth 1 the queued reading is the isolated one: true
a caller floor above the calibration's is topped up with exactly the missing launches: true
a reused window is judged for contention whole: true
a batching depth reuses nothing and dispatches its whole window: true

== Metal queued contention retry ==
a transiently contended Metal window retries once and admits the fresh window: true
persistent Metal contention retries once and remains refused: true
recovered and refused retries each count one discarded first window: true
the returned window excludes the discarded samples and accounts for every launch: true
cc queued contention gets no extra dispatches: true
contended isolated timing never retries and dispatches exactly its 16 samples: true
contended CUDA and HIP queued timing calibrates but takes no retry: true
a refused reused depth-one window retries with fresh singles: true
an admitted Metal window gets no retry or extra dispatches: true
a degenerate clock is refused without a contention retry: true

== the no-verdict fallback is wall-bounded ==
an unresolved calibration never settles on a batch whose launch work exceeds the target: true
a slow candidate whose fits never resolve is timed at depth 1, as isolated times it: true
a candidate owed a batch that measured none within the target is refused, not timed isolated: true
a fallback that kept a batch measured within the target is admitted: true
a slow candidate's unresolved calibration costs no more than its probes: true

== calibration probes are wall-budgeted ==
no calibration probe but the rescue starts once the probes' wall has reached the budget: true
a rescue probe is the calibration's last: true
a stall retry is not started once the stalled confirmation has spent the budget: true
a converging calibration is untouched by the budgets: every probe takes all twelve minima: true
a converging calibration still reaches its affine target depth: true
a 64 ms candidate's depth-2 confirmation stops at three minima: true
a slow candidate's superlinear first pair fits within the wall-relative tolerance: true
a resolved calibration never settles on a batch whose launch work exceeds the target: true
a refitted crossing never settles past the batches it was checked against: true
no calibration settles deeper than queue_depth_projection_factor times the deepest batch it probed: true
the last validation's projection past its deepest probe is capped at the bound: true
a confirmation scaled from below the target is capped at the bound: true
a kernel with a queue threshold below its provisional depth is rescued, timed within the target: true
a refusal no rescue could lift carries its own reason, apart from the contention verdict: true
the longest calibration path dispatches queue_calibration_max_probes probes: true
the longest calibration path is the provisional probe, four validations, a confirmation, its stall retry, a sampled crossing and the rescue: true
the longest calibration path's rescue probes rescue_depth and times the candidate there: true
every synthetic device's dispatches stay within time_routine's documented maximum: true
every reported probe is exactly the batches the device dispatched for it: true

== autotune_timing spelling ==
"queued" selects the queued objective: true
"isolated" selects the isolated objective: true
the spelling is case- and space-insensitive: true
a misspelling is refused rather than defaulted: true

== the instrument's two modes ==
both modes returned a positive finite per-launch time or reported contention: true
isolated timing either reports contention or dispatches one launch per timed run: true
isolated timing reports batch depth 1: true
queued timing either refuses contention or dispatches whole batches at the reported depth: true
isolated timing reuses no calibration: true
queued timing either reports contention or dispatches more launches than isolated: true
both readings are anchored on the timed window they reported: true
isolated reading is a per-launch time or reports contention: PASS
queued reading is a per-launch time rather than a per-batch one, or reports contention: true
queued reading is not that per-launch time divided by the batch depth as well, or reports contention: true
queued timing does not read above isolated timing or reports contention: PASS
queued timing either reports contention or stays within the 64-batch dispatch cap: true

== the objective in the cache key ==
the cache key is stable within one objective: true
the cache key separates the two timing objectives: true
CUDA and HIP queued keys carry the new timing-policy generation: true
cc and Metal queued keys retain their unchanged timing generation: true
an omitted objective keys as the configured one: true
the key's objective spelling round-trips through the mode: true
